# {{ site.name }}

> {{ site.description }}

{{ site.name }} is {{ site.job_title }} and Head of the Mathematical Finance Section in the Department of Mathematics at Imperial College London. He co-leads the Imperial Centre of Excellence in Quantitative Finance and is Director of the CFM-Imperial Institute of Quantitative Finance. He previously held faculty positions at Carnegie Mellon University, the University of Michigan and ETH Zürich. He received his PhD from TU München (2009).

Research interests: {{ site.research_interests | join(", ") }}. Recurring topics: price impact, optimal execution, market making and liquidity provision, transaction costs, portfolio choice, equilibrium asset pricing with frictions, FX fixing.

Contact: {{ site.email }}

